# Tailwind rules

Never write custom CSS classes or selectors. Always use Tailwind utility classes to construct visuals.

- Build all visual styling with Tailwind classes directly in markup.
- If a visual pattern is reusable, extract it into a Svelte component instead of a CSS class.
- The only acceptable custom CSS in the root CSS file is theme configuration (`@theme`), base layer resets (`@layer base`), and `@font-face` declarations.
- Use Svelte 5 `class={[...]}` arrays of literal class strings; do not build class strings via concatenation or template literals.
